"### 涩川春海（安井算哲／保井算哲）与《天文汇钞》星表\n"
"\n"
"涩川春海（渋川 春海，1639—1715）是日本江户时代初期的天文学家，德川幕府首任天文官，也是日本第一部独立历法《贞享历》的制定者。他的姓名在其一生中几经变更：出生于围棋世家安井家，初名安井算哲（二世），后因改姓保井而称保井算哲，晚年改姓涩川，号春海。\n"
"\n"
"春海早年继承家业学习围棋，但中年后全身心投入天文历算。1684年，他受命编制新历，深入研读中国元代郭守敬的《授时历》，并结合实测数据，于1685年完成《贞享历》，取代了在日本沿用八百余年的中国《宣明历》，标志着日本历法开始走向独立。同年，他被任命为首任幕府天文方。\n"
"\n"
"涩川春海深知，历法的精准依赖于可靠的星图与恒星坐标。在编制历法前后的数十年间，他广泛搜集中国历代星图，绘制了多幅影响深远的星图。早期作品如1670年的《天象列次之图》和1677年的《天文分野之图》，主要参考了朝鲜所刻的中国星图《天象列次分野之图》（1395年）。但他并非简单摹写，而是参照黄鼎编纂的《天文大成管窥辑要》（1645年）等文献，对星图进行了系统性修正，包括校正二十八宿距星的误认、调整“弧”“轩辕”等星官的形态，以及移动“狼”“老人”等亮星的位置。\n"
"\n"
"春海星图创作中最关键的转折点，是他于1690年代获得了中国元代星表（即《三垣列舍入宿去极集》，也就是《天文汇钞》星表）的抄本。据竹迫忍的研究，春海在晚期星图中所采用的恒星数据，与元代星表的坐标在岁差校正后几乎完全吻合。在1698年完成的《天文瓊統》星表中，600余颗被成功证认的中国恒星中，绝大多数坐标都与元代星表高度一致。他之所以如此倚重这份星表，根本原因在于其精度极高——元代星表使用0.1度分度值，误差仅0.1度左右，远超春海此前接触的任何资料。\n"
"\n"
"<br><img height=\"600\" src=\"illustrations/sanyuanlieshe2.png\"/> <img height=\"600\" src=\"illustrations/tenmon_kyuto1.png\"/>\n"
"\n"
"*左图：中国《天文汇钞》星图和星表*\n"
"\n"
"*右图：春海的《天文琼统》星图和星表*\n"
"\n"
"春海继承了中国元代星表最为独特的呈现方式：他在《天文琼统》和《天文成象》（1699年）中采用了“图表结合”的形式，即每个星官图形内绘制星点，并在大部分星点下方直接标注入宿度与去极度数值。这种形式在中国古代星表中已属孤例，在日本天文学史上更是独一无二。此外，他在中国传统283星官体系之外，增设了61个日本原创星官、共308颗星，其命名多参考江户时期的日本官制，体现了将中国天学传统与日本本土观测相融合的独创性。\n"
"\n"
"涩川春海还制作了日本最早的天球仪，其中一具于1690年奉纳于伊势神宫，至今仍为重要文化遗产。\n"
"\n"
"<br><img width=\"1000\" src=\"illustrations/tenmon_kyuto2.png\"/>\n"
"\n"
"*涩川春海《天文琼统》星表中记录的座标位置。绿色十字代表中国星官，黄色十字代表春海新增的61个日本星官*\n"
"\n"
"### 关于东亚星空文化星座编号的说明\n"
"\n"
"中国、日本、朝鲜使用同一套星官体系，其汉字写法基本相同，但英文翻译会有差异，各地的发音也完全不同。考虑到东亚星空文化星官的特殊一致性，有必要设置一个完全相同的字段作为主键，用来标示不同文化间相同的星官，这有助于依托Stellarium开展进一步的比较文化研究。\n"
"\n"
"根据Stellarium的规范，星座编号应使用读音缩写以便于记忆，而不应使用纯数字编号。但如前所述，将星座编号作为东亚星空文化间统一的主键是一个更合适的选择。因此，决定使用数字编号而非发音缩写——因为各地发音不同，而且已有专门的`pronounce`字段，无需再做一个重复反映发音的编号。\n"
"\n"
"当前东亚文化星座编号的顺序取自唐代的中国星座诗歌《步天歌》。这首诗歌广为流传，其记录的星官顺序也被视为约定俗成的规范。具体而言，全部283个星座按照三垣和二十八宿分为31组。三垣分别以字母P（紫微垣）、S（太微垣）、H（天市垣）开头，垣内的星座用数字编号；二十八宿则相反，以数字开头（从01至28），宿内的星座用字母命名，例如01A表示角宿的第一个星官。\n"
"\n"
"日本新增的星官全部依据《天文琼统》星图的顺序，使用数字编号，以字母“J”开头，即J01至J61。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of Central Affairs
msgid ""
"This ministry was the highest administrative body in the ancient Japanese "
"government, responsible for the Imperial family's affairs and the "
"administration of the court."
msgstr "中务省：日本古代政府的最高行政机关，负责处理皇室事务以及宫廷的行政管理。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of Ceremonies
msgid ""
"Responsible for the management of the court rank system, personnel records, "
"and the oversight of rites and ceremonies held within the imperial palace."
msgstr "式部省：负责管理宫廷位阶制度、人事档案，以及监督皇宫内举行的祭祀与礼仪。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of Civil
#. Administration
msgid ""
"In charge of the administration of court rituals, the management of temples "
"and shrines, and the oversight of the Buddhist clergy."
msgstr "治部省：负责宫廷礼仪的管理、寺院与神社的事务，以及对佛教教团的监督。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of Popular Affairs
msgid ""
"Managed the census, taxes, civil engineering projects, and the general "
"welfare of the common populace under the Ritsuryō system."
msgstr "民部省：在律令制下管理户籍、税收、土木工程以及一般平民的福祉。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of Military
#. Affairs
msgid ""
"Overseeing the defense and military structure of the nation, including the "
"mobilization of soldiers and the management of military records."
msgstr "兵部省：负责国家的防御与军事体制，包括士兵的动员及军事档案的整理。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of Justice
msgid ""
"Responsible for the administration of laws, the conduct of trials, and the "
"maintenance of order and security within the capital."
msgstr "刑部省：负责法律的执行、审判的进行，以及维持京城内部的秩序与治安。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of Finance
msgid ""
"Managed the national treasury, including taxation, currency, and the "
"distribution of salaries to government officials."
msgstr "大藏省：管理国家财政，包括赋税、货币，以及政府官员俸禄的分配。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Ministry of the Imperial
#. Household
msgid ""
"Dedicated to the management of the private affairs of the Imperial family, "
"including the maintenance of the palace grounds and services for the "
"Emperor."
msgstr "宫内省：专门负责皇室的私务，包括维护宫殿设施及为天皇提供各项服务。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Tutor to the Crown Prince
msgid ""
"Representing the figures responsible for the education, guidance, and "
"character development of the next Emperor."
msgstr "东宫傅：象征负责下一任天皇的教育、指导与品格培养的职官。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Lady of the Bedchamber
msgid ""
"A high-ranking lady in waiting who served the Emperor within the Inner "
"Palace and held significant political influence."
msgstr "御息所：在内宫伺候天皇的高位女官，具有极高的政治影响力。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Palace Table Office
msgid ""
"Responsible for the preparation and management of food and banquet services "
"for the court and official functions."
msgstr "大膳：负责为朝廷的礼仪及官方宴会准备膳食及管理相关膳食事务。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Inner Palace Table Office
msgid ""
"Focusing specifically on the preparation of meals served directly to the "
"Emperor and the Empress within the private residential quarters."
msgstr "内膳：专门负责为天皇及皇后在私人起居空间内准备餐点。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Department of Divinities
msgid ""
"A government agency that operated outside the standard civil ministries, "
"dedicated to the administration of Shinto rites and ancestral worship."
msgstr "神祇官：处于常规行政体系之外的官厅，专门负责管理神道祭祀及祖先崇拜。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Celestial Sail
msgid ""
"Symbolizing the movement and navigation of heavenly bodies across the sky, "
"often associated with the imperial transition."
msgstr "天帆：由天船星官衍生而来，与天船共同构成帆船的形象。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Major Captain
msgid ""
"Refers to a high-ranking military officer who commanded the Imperial Guards "
"and held significant influence in the imperial court."
msgstr "大将：指统领近卫府的高级军事将领，在朝廷中拥有相当大的影响力。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Middle Captain
msgid ""
"A mid-level military official in the Imperial Guard divisions, serving as a "
"vital link in the command structure of the capital."
msgstr "中将：近卫府中的中层武官，在京城的指挥体系中担任重要环节。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Minor Captain
msgid ""
"A junior officer rank in the Imperial Guard, often held by young nobles as a"
" stepping stone in their political careers."
msgstr "少将：近卫府的初级军官职衔，常由年轻贵族担任，是政治生涯的起步点。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Onmyō
msgid ""
"The government department responsible for divination, astronomy, calendar-"
"making, and protection against spiritual misfortunes."
msgstr "阴阳寮：负责占卜、天文、历法制定以及辟邪除祟的政府部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Councilor
msgid ""
"Represents high-ranking advisors who participated in the Council of State to"
" assist the Emperor in national policy."
msgstr "宰相：代表协助天皇制定国家政策的太政官高位顾问。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Pacification Command
#. Headquarters
msgid ""
"Historically referred to regional military commands tasked with the "
"pacification and administration of frontier areas."
msgstr "镇守府：历史上指负责边疆地区平定与行政的区域性军事指挥机构。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Director of Market
msgid ""
"An official in charge of regulating commerce, market prices, and the "
"standard of goods within the capital's designated market areas."
msgstr "市正：在天市垣中，负责管理京城内指定市场区域的商业运作、商品价格及贸易标准的官员。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Military Inspector
msgid ""
"An official designated to oversee military readiness and report on the "
"discipline and status of provincial troops."
msgstr "军监：被指定监督军事准备状态，并汇报地方部队纪律与现状的官员。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Left Division of Outer
#. Palace Guards
msgid ""
"The guard division responsible for the security of the palace, specifically "
"the areas on the left side of the Imperial precinct."
msgstr "左卫门：负责皇宫安全，特别是负责皇宫左侧区域守卫的军事单位。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Celestial Lake
msgid ""
"A symbolic heavenly body representing a reservoir or source of water in the "
"sky, vital for the cultivation of the realm."
msgstr "天湖：与亢池星官有关，象征天空中水库或水源的星象，对领土的耕作至关重要。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Imperial Bath Matron
msgid ""
"A high-ranking attendant responsible for the ritual purification and bathing"
" of the infant imperial family members."
msgstr "汤母：与天乳星官有关，负责为年幼皇族进行仪式性沐浴及洗浴的高级女官。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Imperial Bath Attendant
msgid ""
"The staff responsible for the physical preparation and assistance during the"
" ritual bathing procedures for the court."
msgstr "汤座：与天乳星官有关，负责协助宫廷仪式性沐浴过程中的物理准备及辅助工作的职员。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Mistress of Staff
msgid ""
"A female official who acted as a messenger and intermediary between the "
"Emperor and the court, holding significant administrative authority."
msgstr "内侍：充当天皇与朝廷之间信使及中介的女官，拥有重要的行政权力。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Court Lady
msgid ""
"Lower-ranking women in the service of the palace, performing tasks ranging "
"from cleaning to assisting noblewomen."
msgstr "采女：宫中地位较低的侍女，从清洁打扫到协助贵族女性，执行各种日常杂务。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Trout
msgid ""
"Named after the river fish, this constellation likely reflects the cultural "
"importance of the imperial food supply and seasonal tributes."
msgstr "腹赤：鱼名，鳟鱼的别称。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Celestial Silkworm
msgid ""
"Representing the origins of sericulture, a vital industry in ancient Japan "
"that produced the silk worn by the nobility."
msgstr "天蚕：代表蚕桑业的起源，这是古代日本生产贵族丝绸织物的重要产业。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Right Capital
msgid ""
"Refers to the western division of the ancient capital (Heian-kyō), an area "
"centered on administration and housing."
msgstr "右京：指古代京城（平安京）的西侧区域，是以行政与居住为中心的地区。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Left Capital
msgid ""
"Refers to the eastern division of the ancient capital, which was "
"historically the more prestigious and developed side of the city."
msgstr "左京：指古代京城的东侧区域，历史上是城市中地位更高、开发更完善的一侧。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Office of Imperial Tombs
msgid ""
"Responsible for the maintenance, protection, and ritual care of the tombs of"
" past Emperors and noble families."
msgstr "诸陵：负责历代天皇及贵族陵墓的维护、保护及祭祀工作。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Right Division of Bureau of
#. Horses
msgid ""
"A government office that managed the imperial stables and horses "
"specifically assigned to the western division."
msgstr "右马寮：负责管理御厩及专门分配给右京区域马匹的政府部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Outer Palace Guard
msgid ""
"A general term for the military units responsible for maintaining security "
"around the outer boundaries of the imperial palace."
msgstr "外卫：负责维护皇宫外围安全军事单位的总称。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Left Division of Bureau of
#. Horses
msgid ""
"A government office responsible for the management and care of the horses in"
" the eastern division of the imperial palace."
msgstr "左马寮：负责管理与照料皇宫左侧区域马匹的政府部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Accounting
msgid ""
"An office that audited and managed the state budgets, expenditures, and the "
"overall balance of government finances."
msgstr "主计：负责审核与管理国家预算、支出及政府财政收支平衡的部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Military Stores
msgid ""
"An office responsible for the storage, maintenance, and distribution of "
"military weapons, armor, and equipment."
msgstr "兵库：负责武器、盔甲及其他军需品储存、维护与分发的部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Celestial Rice Bale
msgid ""
"A symbol of prosperity and the agrarian basis of the nation, representing "
"the collection of rice as tax."
msgstr "天俵：繁荣与国家农本思想的象征，代表作为税收征收的米俵。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Taxation
msgid ""
"Managed the collection of agricultural taxes and handled the administration "
"of national revenue."
msgstr "主税：管理农业税征收并处理国家岁入行政的部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Palace
#. Storehouses
msgid ""
"Responsible for the management of the palace's dry goods, grains, and other "
"essential supplies required for court life."
msgstr "大炊：负责管理宫廷内的干货、谷物及日常运作必需品的部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Pine and Bamboo
msgid ""
"Plants often used as symbols of longevity and constancy, reflecting the "
"desired stability of the Imperial court."
msgstr "松竹：常作为长寿与坚贞的象征，反映了对皇朝稳定的期许。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Wild Geese
msgid ""
"A migratory bird constellation reflecting the changing seasons and the "
"traditional observations of nature by the court."
msgstr "鸿雁：候鸟星象，在天苑中，反映了季节的更迭及朝廷对自然规律的传统观察。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Miscanthus × Giganteus
msgid ""
"A tall grass native to Japan, symbolizing the autumnal landscape and the "
"natural beauty favored by the nobility."
msgstr "荻薄：日本原生的长草，象征秋季景色及贵族所喜爱的自然之美。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Celestial Shaft
msgid ""
"Represents the structural axle or support, potentially symbolizing the "
"central governance of the state."
msgstr "天辕：与五车星官有关，代表构造上战车的轴心或支撑。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Dazaifu
msgid ""
"The administrative center for the Kyushu region, which served as a crucial "
"site for diplomacy with foreign lands."
msgstr "太宰府：九州地区的行政中心，也是与周边国家进行外交的重要据点。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Senior Assistant
msgid ""
"A high-ranking administrative post within the Dazaifu, responsible for "
"regional policy and border defense."
msgstr "大贰：太宰府内的高级行政职位，负责地方政策及边境防御。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Junior Assistant
msgid ""
"A subordinate official in the Dazaifu administration who assisted the senior"
" leadership in governing the region."
msgstr "小贰：太宰府行政体系中负责协助高层领导管理地方的下级官员。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Foreign Affairs
#. and Buddhism
msgid ""
"Handled diplomatic relations with foreign envoys and supervised the affairs "
"of Buddhist temples."
msgstr "玄蕃：负责处理外国使节的外交关系，并监管佛教寺院事务的部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Great-grandson
msgid ""
"A symbolic constellation representing the lineage of the Imperial family and"
" the importance of succession."
msgstr "曾孙：丈人、子、孙星官的延续。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Great-great-grandson
msgid ""
"Representing the extended genealogy and the continuity of the imperial "
"bloodline over multiple generations."
msgstr "玄孙：丈人、子、孙星官的延续。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Open Quiver
msgid ""
"A traditional military accessory used for carrying arrows, symbolizing the "
"readiness and defensive posture of the state."
msgstr "箙：与弧矢星官有关，一种传统的装箭军事器具。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Closed Quiver
msgid ""
"A protected case for arrows, representing the disciplined storage and "
"control of military armaments."
msgstr "胡箓：与弧矢星官有关，一种用于存放箭矢的保护容器。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Hayato (Southern Barbarian
#. Guard)
msgid ""
"Refers to warriors from southern Japan who were famous for their specialized"
" skills and service in the Imperial palace."
msgstr "隼人：指来自日本南部、以特殊技能及守卫皇宫而闻名的勇士。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Higher Education
msgid ""
"The imperial university dedicated to training the sons of the aristocracy in"
" Confucian classics and governance."
msgstr "大学寮：旨在培养贵族子弟学习儒家经典与治国之道的帝国大学。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Water Supply
msgid ""
"Responsible for the management and purification of the water supply used for"
" the Emperor’s consumption and daily needs."
msgstr "主水：负责管理与净化天皇日常饮用水及生活用水供应的部门。"

#. Description of Japanese Yasui Map constellation Bureau of Textiles
msgid ""
"An office in charge of the production and weaving of high-quality fabrics "
"and garments for court officials."
